      "id": "reading",
      "className": "panel",
      "type": "rich",
      "html": "<span class=\"number\">INPUT · 4 MIN</span><h2>Read, listen to your own voice, and notice</h2><p class=\"instruction\">Read once for meaning. Then read aloud; on the second pass, notice how the speaker uses whole phrases.</p><div class=\"reading\">I think shorter meetings help our team. The main reason is that everyone needs time to focus. Long meetings often feel less useful. This is because people repeat the same points. For example, our daily meeting now takes fifteen minutes, and we still share the important updates. A good example is yesterday's meeting: we named one blocker and agreed who would help. That's why I prefer a short meeting with a clear purpose. In my opinion, difficult questions can go into a separate conversation. We can try this for a week and compare how much useful work we finish.</div>"
    },
